# OpenCode commands

The root `just opencode` recipe links this directory to `~/.config/opencode/commands/`. OpenCode discovers `.md` files as slash commands and reloads them automatically. This README and the reference files deliberately have no `.md` suffix, so they do not become commands.

## /split

Install with `just opencode`, then run `/split` in an OpenCode session inside a Herdr pane. It forks the current conversation into a pane on the right, reports the new session ID, and tells the fork to wait for instructions. It leaves both sessions in the same working directory.

Requires `uv`, `opencode` using its shared local service, `hc`, and a reachable Herdr app control socket. If OpenCode runs on the same machine as the app, the script uses `herdr-app.sock` in Herdr's app home (`$HERDR_APP_HOME`, or `herdr-app` under `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}`). If OpenCode runs on a VM, forward the desktop's socket to a private path on the VM and export `HERDR_APP_SOCKET` in the VM's shell startup so both the original pane and the fork see it. For example, from the desktop:

```sh
ssh -N -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes -R /absolute/private/path/herdr-app.sock:"$HOME/.config/herdr-app/herdr-app.sock" vm-us
```

Use a directory only your VM account can access: the socket can control the desktop window and launch programs. Use the socket for the Herdr app window that contains your pane.

## /retro

Run `/retro` to review the current coding session, or `/retro <session log or focus>` to specify another session or a focus. It proposes improvements to the agent's environment, ordered by severity, and waits for your selection before changing anything. It runs in the current session so it can use the conversation history.

Source attribution, acquisition details, pinned upstream links, and adaptations are recorded in `retro.md` under the YAML frontmatter's `metadata.provenance` field.

### Updating the upstream copy

Choose an upstream commit, read the source files listed in `metadata.provenance.sources` at that revision, and compare them with the local copies. Preserve the documented OpenCode adaptations and license notice. Update the provenance metadata when refreshing the copy.
